# Aetherion (Drident) — Cursor Rules

## Product Vision

AI-native decision workspace for regulated financial advisory firms. Advisors manage cases, generate compliance-ready recommendations with verified citations, and produce IDD-compliant documentation — with AI handling the heavy lifting and deterministic code handling the math.

Starting market: Swedish occupational pension advisory. Expanding to: life insurance, wealth management, benefits consulting.

## Architecture

Monolithic FastAPI backend + Next.js 14 frontend. PostgreSQL + pgvector. Multi-tenant (org-scoped). Enterprise-grade: PII encryption, audit trails, configurable LLM endpoints.

## Tech Stack

- **Backend:** Python 3.11+ / FastAPI / SQLAlchemy (async) / Alembic
- **Frontend:** Next.js 14 (App Router) / React / TypeScript / shadcn/ui (New York) / Tailwind CSS
- **Database:** PostgreSQL 16 + pgvector
- **LLM:** Anthropic Claude API — two-pass: tool_use (structured output) + Citations API (verified evidence)
- **Embeddings:** Voyage AI (primary), OpenAI (fallback), hash-based (dev). Planned: local HuggingFace (KBLab Swedish model)
- **Auth:** WorkOS (backend integrated), dev bypass via X-Dev-User-Id / X-Dev-Org-Id headers
- **Doc generation:** python-docx, WeasyPrint, Jinja2
- **PDF extraction:** pdfplumber
- **Testing:** pytest + pytest-asyncio + httpx (177+ tests)
- **Infra:** Docker Compose (dev), Azure EU-region (prod, planned)

